		(uuid "35a278d2-0d78-4039-a5cd-da0f6fcc9204")
	)
	(text "TWO-RANGE POWER MONITOR via two I2C device current monitor devices\n\nU1103/INA226 with the 50 mΩ R1101 provides low-loss normal-current\nmeasurement. U1104/INA228 with the 1 Ω R1102 provides more sensitive\nmeasurement of small sleep currents.\n\nTARGET_LOW_RANGE_EN requests the sleep-current range.\nLOW_RANGE_OK_N acts as a hardware safety check and restores the normal\nrange if the current becomes too high. R1102 is bypassed by default.\n\nSee ReusableHarnessRevA_DesignBaseline.md,\nPC02 — Target 5 V switch and two-range power monitor."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 306.07 138.43 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3cc881af-c1b4-4772-a0c8-e0a05b642085")
	)
	(text "U1102 drives LOW_SHUNT_BYPASS_GATE towards EXT_5V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 238.76 270.51 0)
		(effects
